IMPORT prelude

-- Immigration Act 1959 (Singapore) -- a citizen's foreign spouse: what the Act says about her pass and about her
-- permanent residence. s 2 ("pass", "permanent resident of Singapore", "regulations"), s 6(1)(c) (entry on a pass),
-- s 7(1) (citizens need no permit or pass), s 8(2)(b) and (3)(a) (prohibited immigrants), ss 9B and 9C (visas), s 10
-- (entry permits: who applies, the Controller's "may", what the permit authorises, conditions and notice), s 12 (the
-- wife's endorsement), s 14(3) (mandatory cancellation), s 55(1)(c) (passes are made by regulations) and s 57C(6)
-- ("immigration advantage").
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 30/9/2026), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/IA1959.txt (amendments to Act 31 of 2023, Act 5 of 2025 and Act 16 of 2026).
--
-- WHY. Added on 12 October 2026 for REQ-0286 (Haziq scenario, event h033): "A citizen marries a Malaysian national. On
-- what basis is she given a long-term visit pass, and on what basis and after how long may she be granted permanent
-- residence?" "She" is read as the Malaysian spouse, the non-citizen who needs the pass.
--
-- WHAT THE ACT TURNS OUT TO SAY. Nothing about spouses, long-term visit passes or a qualifying period. A "pass" is
-- whatever the regulations create (s 2, s 55(1)(c)); permanent residence is an entry permit the Controller "may" issue
-- on an application in the form the Controller requires and on payment of the prescribed fee (s 10(1), (2)). No length
-- of residence and no marriage appears in s 10.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the Immigration Regulations themselves (the classes of pass, the long-term visit pass, its conditions,
-- validity and cancellation, and the prescribed fees) -- not retrieved; the Minister's list of visa-exempt countries
-- (s 9B(2)) -- not in the Act; ICA's published criteria for a spouse's LTVP or PR -- policy, not law; citizenship by
-- registration (the Constitution, not this Act); re-entry permits and automatic cancellation (ss 11, 14A -- in
-- imm-entry-status.l4); the s 57C offence itself (in imm-offences.l4).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Immigration Act 1959 -- a citizen's spouse: passes and permanent residence`

§§ `2, 55(1)(c) -- where each status comes from`

-- s 2: "'pass' means a pass issued under the regulations entitling the holder thereof to remain, or enter and remain,
-- temporarily in Singapore"; "'regulations' means regulations made under this Act".
-- s 55(1)(c): the Minister may make regulations "providing for and regulating matters relating to permits, passes
-- (including classes of passes) and certificates", including the Controller's powers "relating to an application for and
-- the issue of a permit, pass or certificate, and the cancellation of a pass", the validity period, and conditions.
-- s 10(1): "A non-citizen who wishes to be a permanent resident of Singapore must apply for an entry permit in such form
-- and manner as the Controller requires." s 10(2): "the Controller may issue to the applicant an entry permit".
--
-- The Act names no class of pass at all. A "long-term visit pass" is not a term of the Act; if it exists, it exists in
-- the regulations (or in the Controller's practice under them).
DECLARE Instrument IS ONE OF
    `this Act`
    `regulations under section 55`
    `the Controller's requirements`

GIVETH AN Instrument
`the instrument that creates a long-term visit pass` MEANS `regulations under section 55`

GIVETH AN Instrument
`the instrument that empowers a grant of permanent residence` MEANS `this Act`

GIVETH AN Instrument
`the instrument that sets the form of a permanent residence application` MEANS `the Controller's requirements`

GIVETH AN Instrument
`the instrument that empowers the cancellation of a pass` MEANS `regulations under section 55`

-- s 2: a pass entitles the holder to remain "temporarily". Whatever its length, a pass is never permanent residence.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a pass lets the holder remain permanently` MEANS FALSE

§§ `2, 10 -- permanent residence is an entry permit the Controller may issue`

-- s 2: "'permanent resident of Singapore' means the holder of a valid entry permit".
-- s 10(1): only "a non-citizen who wishes to be a permanent resident" applies. s 10(2): "Upon an application made under
-- subsection (1) and on payment of the prescribed fee, the Controller MAY issue". No minimum period of residence, no
-- marriage, no family tie and no other criterion appears in s 10. The Act makes the grant discretionary in every case
-- and of right in none.
DECLARE Footing IS ONE OF
    `not available`
    `discretionary`
    `as of right`

DECLARE Applicant HAS
    `is a citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is married to a citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has applied in the form the Controller requires` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has paid the prescribed fee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a prohibited immigrant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `years lived in Singapore` IS A NUMBER
    `holds a passport of a country the Minister has approved` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the applicant` IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A Footing
`the footing for permanent residence of` `the applicant` MEANS
    IF `the applicant`'s `is a citizen`
    THEN `not available`
    ELSE IF `the applicant`'s `has applied in the form the Controller requires`
            AND `the applicant`'s `has paid the prescribed fee`
         THEN `discretionary`
         ELSE `not available`

-- No period is stated anywhere in the Act. The figure below is the Act's minimum, not ICA's practice.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum years of residence the Act requires for permanent residence` MEANS 0

GIVEN `the applicant` IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the applicant has met every condition the Act sets for permanent residence` IF
        NOT `the applicant`'s `is a citizen`
    AND `the applicant`'s `has applied in the form the Controller requires`
    AND `the applicant`'s `has paid the prescribed fee`
    AND `the applicant`'s `years lived in Singapore` AT LEAST `the minimum years of residence the Act requires for permanent residence`

-- s 14(3): "Where at any time during the period of validity of any permit ... the Controller is satisfied that the holder
-- ... is a prohibited immigrant, the Controller MUST cancel the permit". INFERENCE (not in s 10): an entry permit issued
-- to a prohibited immigrant would have to be cancelled at once, so in practice it is not issued.
GIVEN `the applicant` IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an entry permit issued to the applicant would have to be cancelled` IF
        NOT `the applicant`'s `is a citizen`
    AND `the applicant`'s `is a prohibited immigrant`

GIVEN `holds a valid entry permit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a permanent resident` IF `holds a valid entry permit`

-- s 10(1A): an entry permit authorises the holder "(a) in the case where the entry permit is issued when the holder is
-- outside Singapore -- to enter Singapore once within the period specified in the conditions of the entry permit; and
-- (b) in any case where the holder has entered or is in Singapore -- to remain in Singapore."
DECLARE Authority IS ONE OF
    `enter once within the period in its conditions`
    `remain in Singapore`

GIVEN `the holder is in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Authority
`what the entry permit authorises` `the holder is in Singapore` MEANS
    IF `the holder is in Singapore` THEN `remain in Singapore` ELSE `enter once within the period in its conditions`

§§ `10(3) to (4A) -- conditions on the entry permit`

-- s 10(3): the Controller may "(a) at the time of issuing ... impose any condition as the Controller thinks fit; or
-- (b) at any time after the issue ... vary or revoke any condition ... or impose any condition thereto." (3A): "whether or
-- not the Controller is entitled to cancel the entry permit". (4): the Controller "must give notice" of the change and the
-- date it takes effect. (4A): for "a class of entry permit holders", where notice to each "is not practicable", the
-- Controller may publish on a prescribed website or in the Gazette, and (4) is then "taken to be satisfied".
DECLARE ConditionChange HAS
    `the holder was given notice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the change is for a class of holders` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Controller assessed individual notice impracticable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the change was published on the website or in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the change` IS A ConditionChange
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice requirement is satisfied` IF
        `the change`'s `the holder was given notice`
    OR  (    `the change`'s `the change is for a class of holders`
         AND `the change`'s `the Controller assessed individual notice impracticable`
         AND `the change`'s `the change was published on the website or in the Gazette`)

§§ `6, 7, 8 -- entering on a pass`

-- s 7(1): "A citizen of Singapore is entitled to enter Singapore without having obtained a permit or pass".
-- s 6(1): a non-citizen must not enter unless "(c) he or she is in possession of a valid pass lawfully issued to him or her
-- to enter Singapore" (or holds a permit, is endorsed, or is exempted).
-- s 8(2)(b): a prohibited immigrant must not enter "unless he or she is in possession of a valid pass in that behalf
-- issuable to a prohibited immigrant under the regulations". s 8(3)(a): a prohibited class includes "any person who is
-- unable to show that he or she has the means of supporting himself or herself and his or her dependants (if any) or that
-- he or she has definite employment awaiting him or her, or who is likely to become a pauper or a charge on the public".
-- Marriage to a citizen exempts the spouse from none of this. (Class (o), the s 9 ban, and s 56 exemptions are left to
-- imm-entry-status.l4.)
DECLARE SpouseEntry HAS
    `is a citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a valid pass` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a prohibited immigrant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the pass is one issuable to a prohibited immigrant` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the entry` IS A SpouseEntry
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the spouse may enter on the pass` IF
        `the entry`'s `is a citizen`
    OR  (    `the entry`'s `holds a valid pass`
         AND (   (NOT `the entry`'s `is a prohibited immigrant`)
              OR `the entry`'s `the pass is one issuable to a prohibited immigrant`))

GIVEN `can show means of support for self and dependants` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `has definite employment awaiting` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is likely to become a charge on the public` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the spouse falls in class (a)` IF
        ((NOT `can show means of support for self and dependants`) AND (NOT `has definite employment awaiting`))
    OR  `is likely to become a charge on the public`

§§ `9B, 9C, 10(2) -- visas`

-- s 9B(1): "a non-citizen must not travel to Singapore (for the purpose of seeking entry under a valid permit or pass)
-- without a Singapore visa that is in effect." (2): not if the traveller "holds and produces a valid passport from a
-- country that is approved by the Minister". The list of approved countries is not in the Act, so whether a Malaysian
-- needs a visa turns on the Minister's approval.
-- s 9C(1): a visa "is not a pass or other permission for, and does not confer any right on, the holder to enter".
-- s 10(2): on issuing an entry permit, the Controller "MUST, if the applicant is required by section 9B(1) to have a
-- Singapore visa, grant a Singapore visa ... and the visa remains valid until the cancellation of the entry permit".
GIVEN `the applicant` IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a Singapore visa is needed to travel` IF
        NOT `the applicant`'s `is a citizen`
    AND NOT `the applicant`'s `holds a passport of a country the Minister has approved`

GIVEN `the applicant` IS AN Applicant, `an entry permit is issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Controller must grant a visa with the entry permit` IF
    `an entry permit is issued` AND `a Singapore visa is needed to travel` `the applicant`

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a visa is itself permission to enter` MEANS FALSE

§§ `12 -- endorsing the wife on the holder's document`

-- s 12: the Controller may, "on application ... by the holder of, or by an applicant for, a permit, pass or certificate,
-- ... endorse upon the permit, pass or certificate issued to that person the name or names of the wife or child of that
-- person." A citizen needs no permit or pass (s 7(1)), so a citizen husband ordinarily holds nothing to endorse; and the
-- section reaches a wife, not a husband. Either way the spouse of a citizen needs her own pass or permit.
DECLARE SpouseSex IS ONE OF
    `a wife`
    `a husband`

GIVEN `the holder holds or is applying for a permit, pass or certificate` IS A BOOLEAN, `the spouse` IS A SpouseSex
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the spouse may be endorsed on the holder's document` IF
        `the holder holds or is applying for a permit, pass or certificate`
    AND CONSIDER `the spouse`
        WHEN `a wife` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `57C(6) -- what counts as an immigration advantage`

-- s 57C(6): "'immigration advantage', in relation to a party to a marriage, means the grant or extension of the validity
-- of any visa, pass, permit or re-entry permit under this Act or the regulations or any order made under this Act for that
-- party or for a child or parent of that party." So a spouse's pass and her entry permit are both immigration advantages,
-- and a marriage entered into to obtain them is within s 57C (offence encoded in imm-offences.l4).
DECLARE Grant IS ONE OF
    `a visa`
    `a pass`
    `an entry permit`
    `a re-entry permit`
    `citizenship`
    `a job`

DECLARE Beneficiary IS ONE OF
    `the party`
    `a child of the party`
    `a parent of the party`
    `a sibling of the party`

GIVEN `the grant` IS A Grant, `the beneficiary` IS A Beneficiary
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the grant is an immigration advantage` IF
        (CONSIDER `the grant`
         WHEN `citizenship` THEN FALSE
         WHEN `a job` THEN FALSE
         OTHERWISE TRUE)
    AND (CONSIDER `the beneficiary`
         WHEN `a sibling of the party` THEN FALSE
         OTHERWISE TRUE)
